Confirmed: SECOND call returns true — module-level /g regex state pollution. Where? In the first isUncitedSpecClaim call: coreClaimText → /[^.!?\n]+/ exec (no g, fine) ... hasVerifiableCitation → hasTrustedDocUrl loop → ends with lastIndex 0.

Hmm wait — who leaves state? DOC_URL_HOST_RE.exec in hasTrustedDocUrl: loop continues while m !== null; ends when exec returns null → lastIndex reset to 0. Not it.

Wait — is it FILE_CITATION_RE? No /g.

Hmm — maybe it's one of SPEC_CLAIM_RES in findSpecClaimPhrase? Not called here (classifyFindingSeverity not in path)... isUncitedSpecClaim path: coreClaimText (LEADING_MARKER_RES replace — replace with non-global regex replaces first match only; fine), /[^.!?\n]+/ exec, isExternalSpecClaim (SPEC_CLAIM_RES .test — no g), hasVerifiableCitation → FILE_CITATION_RE.test, hasTrustedDocUrl → DOC_URL_HOST_RE exec loop.

Actually wait — 'the spec says X (https://github.com/acme/spec)': in hasTrustedDocUrl, first exec matches 'github.com' — trusted → return true IMMEDIATELY, leaving lastIndex at 13 (after 'github.com')! The early return skips the second exec that would reset lastIndex. Next call: exec starts at lastIndex 13 → continues in 'https://github.com/acme/spec)' from position 13 → next match attempt... '/acme/spec' — no https → returns null → resets to 0? But the SECOND call returned true (BUG), meaning it found no match... wait second call returned TRUE = "uncited" = hasVerifiableCitation false. Because exec started at lastIndex=13, scanned rest 'https... wait text is same; from index 13 'hub.com/acme/spec)' — no 'https://' → null → hasTrustedDocUrl returns false. THIRD call: lastIndex reset → matches again.

Fix: reset DOC_URL_HOST_RE.lastIndex = 0 before the loop, or avoid early return:

```js
function hasTrustedDocUrl(text, hosts) {
   DOC_URL_HOST_RE.lastIndex = 0;
   var m = DOC_URL_HOST_RE.exec(text);
   var found = false;
   while (m !== null && !found) {
       if (hostIsTrusted(m[1], hosts)) found = true;
       else m = DOC_URL_HOST_RE.exec(text);
   }
   DOC_URL_HOST_RE.lastIndex = 0;
   return found;
}
```

Simpler: keep loop but set lastIndex=0 at start and end. Also — node direct require didn't show the bug because... it would, on a second call. My node test called only once per string. OK.

Also same class of bug: any other /g module regexes? DOC_URL_HOST_RE is the only /g. Fix it.

